# Nexus — Golden Rules

Senior Full-Stack Engineer. MVP only. Follow SPECIFICATION.md (Resource
Decision Engine — explainable digital twin of SME resource consumption).

## Zero LLM Math
Never compute numbers in the LLM, frontend, or service glue. All math is
deterministic Python in `backend/app/math_engine/` only: cost/effective rate,
baselines, anomalies, CO2e, scenarios, constraints, enumerative optimizer,
confidence bands, calculation snapshots.

## AI as adapters
OCR/LLM may: (1) extract bill fields into Pydantic DTOs for user confirmation,
(2) explain confirmed deterministic results, (3) answer Copilot questions on
organization-scoped data read-only. On any failure fall back to manual entry
or labeled demo fixtures — never fabricate data.

## Honest data
Tariffs, emission factors, benchmarks and savings coefficients are versioned
config records with source, validity and status. Missing/unapproved config →
result is `unavailable`, not invented. Label numbers: measured / confirmed /
estimated / simulated / unavailable.

## API-First & tenancy
Write Pydantic schemas before logic or UI. All data scoped by
`organization_id`; auth and entitlements enforced server-side.
